The fix for #540 is committed and queued to land, but the issue is still open. The land has been queued with the manager since 13:17Z and had no verdict by 16:00Z, when my time ran out. The manager lands it after this run and posts its verdict on the issue, and the next run posts the final comment and closes it.

**What changed** (commit `58ae0c2c`, test only, in `AuthorizerBehaviorTest.java.tmpl`): the check no longer counts JWK watch attempts in a fixed 2.5s after start. It waits up to 30s for three attempts and records when each arrives. It then asserts the gaps are at least 0.5s and then 1s, the backoff schedule's minimums. A slow start only delays the attempts and a slow runner only widens the gaps, so neither can fail it. A source that retries without backoff still does.

**Verification:**
- **No load, `just current-generation-java`:** the Authorizer check passed. That run then failed later in `AccountingSinkDurableTest` ("none were dropped"), which is #341's bug and its fix is already queued. A second run of the same leg passed every Java fixture, including the accounting sink. Its last line was a tree-guard notice, only because I committed while it ran.
- **Under CPU and disk load** (8 CPU spinners and 8 synced disk writers, load average about 22 on 8 cores): passed 10 out of 10 runs.
- **No-backoff mutant** (retry delay patched to 0, checked by hand): the new check fails with "retried 78ms then 21ms …, want at least 500ms then 1000ms".
- **Slow start:** with the first watch started 2s late, the new check passes and the old one fails ("made 0 attempts in 2.5s").
- **Old check not reproduced:** under the same load the old check passed 10 out of 10, so the original flake did not happen here on its own. The 2s delay stood in for the slow start.
- **Not run:** `just gates`. The land runs it, and its verdict will name the gate set.

**Patch:** main has taken features since v2.6.1, so main gets no `v2.6.2` tag. Instead there are backport PRs, each naming the next patch tag to cut once it merges:

| PR | Branch | Tag |
|---|---|---|
| #547 | release/2.0 | v2.0.28 |
| #548 | release/2.1 | v2.1.21 |
| #549 | release/2.2 | v2.2.18 |
| #550 | release/2.3 | v2.3.20 |
| #551 | release/2.4 | v2.4.20 |
| #552 | release/2.5 | v2.5.21 |
| #553 | release/2.6 | v2.6.10 |

`just current-generation-java` passed on the 2.0 and 2.6 backports. The other five are the same change applied cleanly and were not run.

**Trace check (rule 13):** the only handler I touched is the test's fake JWK service, which makes no outgoing calls. `looper-trace check` reports 8 findings, all in `cross-test/server-runtime/client/go/main.go`, which this change does not touch; they are already filed as #311.

The progress comment on #540 has the details.
